package com.linguapro.android

object ScenarioBankB1 {
    private fun s(n: Int, text: String, a: ScenarioQuestion, b: ScenarioQuestion, transfer: String, c: ScenarioQuestion) =
        UnitScenario("B1-U$n", text, a, b, transfer, c)
    val items = listOf(
        s(1, "Our team planned to finish a website on Friday, but the customer requested changes on Thursday. We explained that making the changes would take two extra days. Instead of promising an impossible date, we agreed to show the revised design on Friday and deliver the working site on Monday. I wrote an email afterwards so that everyone had the same record of the agreement.",
            sq("What did the team agree to show on Friday?", "The revised design", "The finished working site", "An unrelated new project", "Cuma tasarım, pazartesi çalışan site teslimi kararlaştırılıyor; ilk plan değişiyor."),
            sq("Why was a follow-up email sent?", "To record the agreement clearly", "To cancel the customer relationship", "To ask for an unknown address", "So that everyone had the same record anlaşmanın ortak kaydını oluşturma amacıdır."),
            "A colleague says Friday is impossible but offers a draft Friday and a final version Monday. The client accepts.",
            sq("Which summary is accurate?", "The draft and final version have different deadlines.", "Everything is due Friday.", "The project was cancelled.", "Draft ve final için iki ayrı tarih var.")),
        s(2, "While I was travelling home, my train stopped between stations. At first, nobody knew what had happened. Then an announcement explained that a signal had failed. I called my family, who were waiting for me at the station. They went to a nearby café instead of standing in the cold. We arrived forty minutes late, but everyone knew where to meet.",
            sq("What caused the delay?", "A signal failure", "The family's café visit", "The passenger's phone call", "Signal had failed gecikmenin nedeni; kafe ziyareti gecikmeye verilen karşılıktır."),
            sq("How did the phone call help?", "The family could wait somewhere warmer.", "It repaired the signal.", "It made the train arrive early.", "Bilgi alan aile soğukta beklemek yerine kafeye geçti; tren arızası değişmedi."),
            "I was cooking when the lights went out. I stopped cooking and called the building manager.",
            sq("Which action happened after the interruption?", "Calling the manager", "Starting to cook", "Turning on the lights successfully", "When ile kesinti, ardından arama anlatılır; ışıkların yeniden açıldığı söylenmez.")),
        s(3, "Some neighbours wanted to turn an empty room into a gym, while others preferred a shared study space. Rather than voting immediately, we listed the needs behind both suggestions. Quiet study mattered during the day; exercise was more popular in the evening. We proposed different uses at different times and agreed to review the arrangement after a month, instead of claiming it would satisfy everyone forever.",
            sq("How did the neighbours address the disagreement?", "By proposing different uses at different times", "By ignoring the study-space request", "By closing the room permanently", "Günün saatlerine göre iki kullanım önerilerek ihtiyaçlar birleştiriliyor."),
            sq("Why will the arrangement be reviewed?", "Its practical success is not yet certain.", "The room has already been sold.", "Everyone rejected both ideas.", "Review after a month, çözümün kalıcı başarı garantisi olmadığını gösterir."),
            "Both groups want access to the room, but at different times. A timetable could meet both needs.",
            sq("What makes the proposed compromise possible?", "The preferred times differ.", "Neither group wants the room.", "The room is being demolished.", "Farklı saatler, ortak mekânı paylaşmayı mümkün kılar.")),
        s(4, "I wanted a job in design, but most advertisements asked for experience. A tutor suggested making a small portfolio rather than sending the same empty application repeatedly. I created three sample projects and asked for feedback. One employer still rejected me, but another invited me to explain my work. The portfolio didn't guarantee a job; it gave me a better way to show what I could do.",
            sq("What did the tutor recommend?", "Creating a portfolio", "Inventing paid work experience", "Applying without showing any work", "Three sample projects gerçek beceriyi göstermeye yarayan portfolyodur; deneyim uydurulmaz."),
            sq("What was the limited benefit of the portfolio?", "It helped demonstrate ability.", "It guaranteed acceptance everywhere.", "It removed every experience requirement.", "Didn't guarantee a job ifadesi faydanın sınırını açıkça belirtir."),
            "The employer liked my examples but said the role needed more experience.",
            sq("Which conclusion follows?", "Positive feedback did not mean an offer.", "An offer was guaranteed.", "The examples were never reviewed.", "Beğenilme ile işe alınma farklı sonuçlardır.")),
        s(5, "A local newspaper reported that the recycling centre might close. The headline sounded final, but the article said the council was still discussing several options. I checked the council's notice before sharing the story. It confirmed that no decision had been made. I shared that detail with my neighbours because a short headline alone could give them the wrong impression.",
            sq("What had the council actually decided?", "No final decision had been made.", "The centre had already closed.", "Recycling had been banned.", "Still discussing ve no decision iki ayrı kanıtla kararın kesinleşmediğini gösterir."),
            sq("Why did the speaker check another source?", "The headline could be misleading.", "The newspaper contained no article.", "The centre had never existed.", "Başlık kesin görünürken ayrıntıda seçenekler tartışılıyordu."),
            "The headline says 'Park to close', but the article says closure is only one proposal.",
            sq("What should a careful summary preserve?", "Closure is a proposal, not a final decision.", "Closure has definitely happened.", "No proposal exists.", "One proposal ile kesin gerçekleşme arasındaki fark korunmalıdır.")),
        s(6, "I sent a message asking a colleague to check a file, but I forgot to include the deadline. She assumed it could wait until next week, while I needed it that afternoon. Once we realised the misunderstanding, I explained the reason for the urgency. She checked the key section first, and I changed my future messages to include both the requested action and the time it was needed.",
            sq("What information was missing from the first message?", "The deadline", "The colleague's name", "The fact that a file existed", "Forgot to include the deadline yanlış beklentiye yol açan eksikliktir."),
            sq("How was the immediate problem handled?", "The key section was checked first.", "The entire project was abandoned.", "The colleague was told to ignore it.", "Key section first acil ihtiyaca yönelik önceliklendirmedir."),
            "Please check page three by two o'clock; we need it for the customer call.",
            sq("Which elements make this request clear?", "Action, deadline and reason", "Only a greeting", "An undefined future task", "Check page three eylem; by two son tarih; customer call gerekçedir.")),
        s(7, "After university, I considered moving to a larger city. There were more jobs there, but rent would be higher and I would be far from my family. A friend suggested trying a short work placement before making a permanent move. I accepted the placement and kept my room at home for the first month. This gave me time to compare daily life in both places.",
            sq("Why did the speaker try a placement first?", "To explore the choice before committing permanently", "To avoid learning about the city", "To guarantee a lifelong contract", "Before making a permanent move, denemeyi karar öncesine koyar."),
            sq("What was one disadvantage of the larger city?", "Higher rent", "No jobs at all", "Living closer to family", "More jobs avantaj; higher rent ve aileden uzaklık dezavantajdır."),
            "I want to try living abroad for a month before deciding whether to move permanently.",
            sq("What role does the short stay play?", "It is a trial before a bigger decision.", "It proves the decision is already permanent.", "It prevents any comparison.", "Before deciding, kalıcı kararın henüz verilmediğini gösterir.")),
        s(8, "The washing machine I bought stopped working after two weeks. I contacted the shop with the receipt and described the fault. The employee first suggested checking the connection, which I had already done. I explained this calmly and asked what the next step would be. She arranged an inspection and gave me a reference number so I could follow up if nobody contacted me.",
            sq("What did the customer ask after explaining the checks?", "What the next step would be", "Whether the employee liked the machine", "How to buy an unrelated appliance", "What the next step would be, çözüm sürecini netleştiren sorudur."),
            sq("Why was a reference number useful?", "It would help with follow-up.", "It immediately repaired the machine.", "It replaced the purchase receipt.", "So I could follow up takip işlemi için numara verildiğini belirtir."),
            "I've already tried restarting it. Could you explain what happens after this fault report?",
            sq("What does the customer seek?", "Information about the next stage", "Instructions they have never tried", "A new job at the shop", "Already tried ile tamamlanan deneme, after ... ile sonraki aşama ayrılır.")),
        s(9, "Our club needed to choose between a cheap venue outside town and a more expensive one near the station. At first, everyone focused on the rental price. Then we included travel costs and the difficulty of getting home late. The central venue became the better choice for most members, even though its advertised price was higher. Two members disagreed, so we recorded their concerns instead of pretending the decision was unanimous.",
            sq("Why did the central venue become preferable?", "Travel costs and access changed the comparison.", "Its rental price was the lowest.", "No one considered transport.", "Toplam maliyet ve ulaşım, yalnızca kira fiyatından farklı bir değerlendirme oluşturdu."),
            sq("Was the decision unanimous?", "No, two members disagreed.", "Yes, everyone supported it.", "There were no members.", "Two members disagreed ifadesi oybirliği olmadığını gösterir."),
            "The cheaper hotel needs a long taxi ride, so we will compare total costs before booking.",
            sq("What is being compared?", "Accommodation plus travel costs", "Room price alone", "Only hotel colours", "Total costs, konaklama ve ulaşımı birlikte değerlendirmeyi gerektirir.")),
        s(10, "I noticed that I felt tired after several evenings of working late. Instead of making a large change all at once, I decided to leave work on time twice a week and keep a regular bedtime. I told my manager about the plan so that late requests could be discussed earlier. After a fortnight, I felt more rested, although busy days still happened.",
            sq("What kind of change did the speaker make?", "A small, planned change to working hours and bedtime", "Leaving the job immediately", "Avoiding all communication with the manager", "Twice a week ve regular bedtime küçük, planlı değişikliklerdir."),
            sq("Did the change remove every busy day?", "No, busy days still happened.", "Yes, work ended completely.", "The text says no change was tried.", "Although ... still happened olumlu sonucun sınırını belirtir."),
            "I feel better with a regular routine, but the busiest days remain difficult.",
            sq("Which summary preserves both points?", "The routine helps without solving everything.", "The routine has no benefit.", "All difficulties have disappeared.", "Helps ve remain difficult iki bilginin de korunması gerekir.")),
        s(11, "We planned to attend an outdoor concert together. When rain was forecast, the organisers moved it into the town hall. The new room had fewer seats, so we were asked to confirm attendance again. One friend couldn't come at the new time. We kept her informed and agreed to meet for a meal another day rather than treating the concert as the only chance to spend time together.",
            sq("Why was attendance confirmed again?", "The new venue had fewer seats.", "The musicians had never been booked.", "Everyone had lost their tickets.", "Fewer seats yeniden katılım sayısının doğrulanmasına gerekçe oluşturur."),
            sq("How did the group respond to the friend's difficulty?", "They planned another occasion to meet.", "They ended the friendship.", "They claimed the time had not changed.", "Another day yemek buluşması, katılamayan arkadaş için alternatif yaratır."),
            "The event moved indoors, but the original tickets remain valid.",
            sq("What changed and what stayed the same?", "The venue changed; tickets stayed valid.", "Tickets were cancelled; the venue stayed the same.", "Nothing changed.", "Moved indoors yer değişikliği; remain valid biletin geçerliliğidir.")),
        s(12, "At my review, the manager praised the quality of my reports but said they sometimes arrived too late. I initially heard only the criticism. After asking for an example, I understood that another team needed the figures before noon. We agreed on an earlier draft deadline and a short check-in. The feedback was not that my work was useless; it identified a useful improvement to the process.",
            sq("What did the feedback mainly ask the speaker to improve?", "The timing of reports", "Every report's content", "The other team's job titles", "Kalite övülüyor; sometimes arrived too late zamanlama sorununu gösteriyor."),
            sq("Why was asking for an example helpful?", "It clarified another team's need.", "It proved all feedback was false.", "It removed the need for a deadline.", "Before noon ihtiyacını anlayarak süreç iyileştirmesi planlandı."),
            "Your analysis is clear, but please send a draft earlier so we can review it.",
            sq("Which interpretation is fair?", "The content is valued; the schedule needs adjustment.", "The analysis is completely rejected.", "No change is requested.", "Clear olumlu içerik değerlendirmesi; send ... earlier zamanlama talebidir.")),
        s(13, "In an interview, I was asked about a time I solved a problem. I described a late delivery at my previous workplace, explained how I contacted the supplier, and said what changed afterwards. I didn't claim to have solved every delay. The interviewer asked which part I had handled personally, so I separated my own actions from the work the whole team had done.",
            sq("Why did the interviewer ask about personal involvement?", "To distinguish the applicant's actions from the team's", "To ask for a different delivery address", "To cancel the interview without explanation", "Handled personally, bireysel katkıyı ekip çalışmasından ayırma sorusudur."),
            sq("What made the account specific?", "It included a problem, actions and a result.", "It only listed vague strengths.", "It claimed there had never been a delay.", "Gecikme, tedarikçiyle iletişim ve sonrasındaki değişim somut bir olay yapısı oluşturur."),
            "We solved the problem together. I checked the figures; my colleague spoke to the client.",
            sq("Which action belongs to the speaker?", "Checking the figures", "Speaking to the client", "Doing every task alone", "I ile checking, my colleague ile client konuşması eşleşir.")),
        s(14, "A colleague sent an urgent request while I was working on another deadline. I couldn't complete both tasks that morning. Rather than simply saying no, I explained my current priority and offered to check the most important page before lunch. She said the remaining pages could wait until tomorrow. We agreed on the smaller task first, which prevented both requests from becoming late.",
            sq("How did the speaker respond to the urgent request?", "By explaining the conflict and offering a limited task", "By promising to finish everything immediately", "By ignoring the colleague", "Mevcut öncelik açıklandı ve en önemli sayfa için sınırlı yardım önerildi."),
            sq("Which work could wait?", "The remaining pages", "The most important page", "Both original deadlines", "Remaining pages could wait until tomorrow deniyor."),
            "I can check the summary today, but the full document will need to wait until tomorrow.",
            sq("What is offered today?", "Checking the summary", "Completing the full document", "Doing no work at all", "Summary bugün; full document yarın ayrımı açıkça yapılır.")),
        s(15, "Two reports described the same local event differently. One focused on the traffic delay, while the other discussed why residents had organised the event. I read both and noticed that they agreed on the time and place. Their emphasis differed, rather than every fact being contradictory. When I told a friend about it, I included the shared facts and explained that the reports highlighted different concerns.",
            sq("How did the reports differ?", "They emphasised different aspects.", "They disagreed on every fact.", "They described events in different cities.", "Emphasis differed ve shared time/place, odak farkını olgu çelişkisinden ayırır."),
            sq("What did the speaker include in the summary?", "Shared facts and the difference in emphasis", "Only the most dramatic headline", "Invented details about the organisers", "Shared facts ile highlighted different concerns birlikte aktarılır."),
            "Both articles say the meeting was on Monday; one focuses on cost and the other on access.",
            sq("What is common to both articles?", "The meeting date", "Their main emphasis", "Every opinion", "Monday ortak tarih; cost ve access farklı odaklardır.")),
        s(16, "I wanted to cook at home more often, but I usually arrived too late to prepare a complicated meal. A friend suggested choosing two simple recipes and buying the ingredients in advance. I tried this for a week. It made evenings easier, although I still ate out once when a meeting ran late. I kept the plan because it was practical, not because I followed it perfectly every day.",
            sq("What made the plan practical?", "Simple recipes and advance preparation", "Cooking complicated meals every night", "Avoiding all planning", "İki basit tarif ve önceden malzeme almak zaman kısıtına uygun çözümdür."),
            sq("Why did the speaker still eat out once?", "A meeting ran late.", "Every recipe failed.", "The friend rejected the plan.", "When a meeting ran late istisnanın gerekçesidir."),
            "The plan helped on most days, even though I missed one evening.",
            sq("Which conclusion is reasonable?", "A useful plan need not be followed perfectly to help.", "Missing once proves the plan was useless.", "The plan was followed every day.", "Most days ve missed one evening birlikte değerlendirilir.")),
        s(17, "I chose an evening course because I work during the day. Before enrolling, I asked whether missed lessons could be watched online. The centre said recordings would be available, but group activities could not be repeated individually. That helped me decide whether the course fitted my schedule. I registered after checking the dates of the group sessions rather than assuming online recordings would replace everything.",
            sq("What was the limitation of recordings?", "They did not replace group activities.", "They were never available.", "They were only for teachers.", "Group activities could not be repeated individually, kayıtların sınırını açıklar."),
            sq("What did the speaker check before registering?", "The dates of group sessions", "Only the building's colour", "The tutor's holiday plans", "Group sessions dates, iş takvimiyle uyumu kontrol etmek içindir."),
            "The lectures are recorded, but attendance is required for the practical workshop.",
            sq("Which part requires being present?", "The practical workshop", "Every recorded lecture", "Neither part", "But, kayıt ile uygulama katılım zorunluluğunu ayırır.")),
        s(18, "I used to drive to work because it seemed quicker. After the town introduced a direct bus, I tried it for a fortnight. The bus journey took ten minutes longer, but I no longer had to search for parking. I also read during the trip. On days when I needed to carry heavy equipment, I still drove, so the change was useful without being an absolute rule.",
            sq("What advantage offset the longer bus journey?", "Not needing to find parking", "A shorter journey every day", "Being able to carry any equipment", "Took longer olsa da parking arama zorunluluğu kalkıyor."),
            sq("When did the speaker still drive?", "When carrying heavy equipment", "On every ordinary day", "Only when reading", "Heavy equipment taşıma durumu istisna olarak belirtilir."),
            "The train takes longer, but I can work on it and avoid parking fees.",
            sq("What kind of comparison is made?", "A trade-off between time and other benefits", "A claim that the train is always faster", "A statement that costs never matter", "Uzun süre ile çalışma olanağı ve park ücretinden kaçınma birlikte değerlendirilir.")),
        s(19, "At the end of the month, I often wondered where my money had gone. I began recording small purchases as well as larger bills. After two weeks, I noticed that unplanned snacks and taxi trips added up. I didn't stop every small treat; I set a weekly amount for them. The record helped me make a choice based on actual spending rather than a vague feeling.",
            sq("What did the spending record reveal?", "Small unplanned purchases added up.", "Large bills did not exist.", "Every taxi journey was free.", "Snacks ve taxi trips birikerek toplam harcamayı etkiliyordu."),
            sq("How did the speaker respond?", "By setting a weekly amount for small treats", "By claiming all treats were forbidden", "By ignoring the record", "Didn't stop every treat, sınırlı bütçe belirlemekle tam yasaklamayı ayırır."),
            "I thought I spent little on taxis, but my record showed several trips each week.",
            sq("What changed the speaker's view?", "Recorded spending", "A guess without evidence", "A promise of free travel", "Record showed, tahminin somut kayıtla değiştiğini gösterir.")),
        s(20, "The film began slowly, and I nearly stopped watching. Halfway through, I realised the early scenes were showing why the main character avoided her family. By the ending, those details mattered more than I had expected. My friend still found the film too slow. We agreed that the acting was strong, even though we disagreed about whether the pace helped the story.",
            sq("Why did the early scenes become important?", "They explained the character's behaviour.", "They contained unrelated advertisements.", "They proved the ending was missing.", "Avoided her family davranışının gerekçesini kuran sahneler olarak yeniden değerlendiriliyor."),
            sq("What did both viewers agree on?", "The acting was strong.", "The pace was ideal.", "The film had no ending.", "We agreed ... acting güçlü ortak nokta; pace üzerinde ayrışıyorlar."),
            "I liked the ending, but my friend found it unconvincing. We both praised the music.",
            sq("Which view is shared?", "Praise for the music", "Approval of the ending", "Dislike of the whole film", "Both praised the music ortak değerlendirmedir.")),
        s(21, "A message offered me a prize and asked me to sign in through a link. It looked like a company I knew, but the address contained an extra word. Instead of using the link, I opened the company's usual site myself and found no prize notice. I deleted the message and told a friend what had made me suspicious, without claiming that every promotional message was necessarily fake.",
            sq("What made the speaker suspicious?", "An unusual address", "A familiar company name alone", "The absence of any link", "Adresin ek kelime içermesi şirket adına benzeyen görüntüden ayrılan ipucudur."),
            sq("How was the claim checked?", "By opening the usual company site independently", "By entering a password in the message link", "By paying for the prize first", "Instead of using the link, bağımsız doğrulama yoludur."),
            "The message looks familiar, but I'll check through the official app before responding.",
            sq("What does the speaker avoid assuming?", "That a familiar appearance proves authenticity", "That checking is impossible", "That every app message is genuine", "Familiar görünüm ile gerçeklik aynı şey kabul edilmiyor.")),
        s(22, "Our building introduced separate bins, but the labels were unclear. Several neighbours put food waste in the wrong container. Rather than blaming them, we asked the manager for clearer signs and examples. After the signs were changed, the mistakes became less frequent. We still checked the local collection guidance because different materials were collected on different days.",
            sq("What contributed to the original mistakes?", "Unclear labels", "A complete lack of bins", "A ban on asking questions", "Labels were unclear, yanlış ayrıştırmanın bağlamdaki nedenidir."),
            sq("What improved after the change?", "Mistakes became less frequent.", "Every collection happened on the same day.", "All materials became identical.", "Less frequent, hataların azaldığını söyler; tamamen yok olduğunu değil."),
            "People confused the two bins, so we added pictures showing suitable items.",
            sq("What was the purpose of the pictures?", "To clarify how to use the bins", "To remove the collection service", "To blame every resident", "Pictures showing suitable items kullanım bilgisini netleştirir.")),
        s(23, "My neighbour played loud music late in the evening. I was annoyed, but I didn't know whether he realised how clearly I could hear it. The next day, I explained the problem and asked if he could lower the volume after ten. He apologised and suggested telling him if it happened again. We agreed on a practical limit rather than arguing about his taste in music.",
            sq("What did the speaker ask for?", "Lower volume after ten", "No music at any time", "A different style of music", "After ten belirli zaman sınırıdır; genel müzik yasağı değildir."),
            sq("How did the neighbour respond?", "He apologised and accepted follow-up.", "He denied that music existed.", "He moved out immediately.", "Apologised ve tell him if it happened again çözüme açık yanıtı gösterir."),
            "I don't mind daytime practice, but could you stop after nine in the evening?",
            sq("What boundary is requested?", "An evening time limit", "A total ban on practice", "Only a change of instrument", "Don't mind daytime, gündüzün kabul edilip akşam sınırı istendiğini gösterir.")),
        s(24, "At the airport, I discovered that my suitcase had not arrived. I went to the baggage desk and gave them the flight number and a description of the case. The employee checked the record and said it was still at the previous airport. I left my contact details and asked how I would receive an update, rather than waiting without knowing the next step.",
            sq("Where was the suitcase according to the record?", "At the previous airport", "At the hotel", "Inside another passenger's car", "Still at the previous airport aranan eşyanın bildirilen yeridir."),
            sq("What did the traveller clarify before leaving?", "How an update would be received", "How to cancel every future flight", "Whether the employee owned the airport", "How I would receive an update takip iletişiminin netleştirilmesidir."),
            "Your bag is on the next flight. Please confirm the address where you want it delivered.",
            sq("What information is requested?", "The delivery address", "The bag's purchase price", "A new passport number", "Address where ... delivered teslimat yeridir.")),
        s(25, "My grandmother taught me a soup recipe, but her instructions used phrases such as a little and until it looks right. When I tried it alone, I wasn't sure how much water to add. We cooked it together again, and I wrote down approximate amounts and the order of the steps. She explained that the amounts could still vary with the vegetables, so the notes were a guide rather than an exact rule.",
            sq("Why were the first instructions difficult to follow?", "Some amounts were unclear.", "No ingredients were named anywhere.", "The grandmother refused to explain.", "A little gibi ifadeler miktarı belirsiz bırakıyordu."),
            sq("How should the written notes be used?", "As a guide with some flexibility", "As an exact rule for every vegetable", "As proof that the recipe cannot work", "Amounts could vary, notların rehber olduğunu belirtir."),
            "Start with a small amount of water and add more if the mixture is too thick.",
            sq("What determines whether more water is needed?", "The thickness of the mixture", "The colour of the notebook", "The number of instructions", "If ... too thick koşulu, su ekleme kararını belirler.")),
        s(26, "I used to say I wanted to read more, but I never made a specific plan. Now I keep a book in my bag and read on two bus journeys each week. I chose a short novel so that finishing it would feel achievable. If I miss a journey, I continue the following week instead of abandoning the goal. The plan is small enough to fit my routine.",
            sq("What makes the new goal more practical?", "A specific time and an achievable book", "A promise to read every book immediately", "Avoiding the usual routine", "İki otobüs yolculuğu ve kısa roman, hedefi uygulanabilir kılar."),
            sq("What happens after a missed session?", "The speaker continues the following week.", "The goal is abandoned permanently.", "The book is replaced automatically.", "Continue ... instead of abandoning sürdürülebilir karşılıktır."),
            "I missed one practice session, so I'll return to the plan tomorrow rather than start from zero.",
            sq("What attitude does this express?", "Resuming after a setback", "Treating one miss as total failure", "Giving up the plan", "Rather than start from zero, aksamanın tüm ilerlemeyi silmediğini ifade eder."))
    )
}
